      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onalaska%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name may honor a Lenape woman named Onalaska who died around 1780, according to local historian George Tabbert.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Onalaska%2C_Wisconsin",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Onalaska Historical Society Museum, housed in the public library, showcases exhibits from the Ice Age to the city’s lumber‑age roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
