      ],
      "source": "https://www.onalaskawi.gov/business_detail_T13_R55.php",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In the 1840s, the railroad helped turn Onalaska into a bustling river town, and the city once hosted the Dakota 400 train service until 1963.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
